<title>AUSTRIA: Austria insolvency liabilities fall 59 pct in H1.</title>
<headline>Austria insolvency liabilities fall 59 pct in H1.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total liabilities of insolvent Austrian firms fell 59 percent in the first six months of the year, Austria's credit watchdog said on Friday in reference to preliminary estimates.</p>
<p>Liabilities fell to 16.1 billion schillings from 39.3 billion in the year-ago period, while the number of insolvencies opened was steady at 1,130 after 1,125 in the first half of 1996, it added. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12256</p>
</text>
